; personality.xon -- what this bundle IS.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every other
; manifest in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon).  A form a reader
; does not know is a loud error, never a skip -- a manifest that silently
; ignores half of itself cannot be extended without wondering which readers
; obeyed which half.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (personality "NAME")        the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a REQUIREMENT, not a taste
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (entry "FILE")              the one self-booting file

(personality "krn")

; HELIUM, and this is derived rather than preferred.  Kernel's imports are
; krn/base and krn/printer; neither reaches past x-core -- no float, no
; socket, no file.  Declaring a heavier dialect would be a lie that costs
; every user a numeric tower they never call.
(dialect he)

; PAIRING, NOT PINNING.  A digest freezes bytes; it says nothing about
; whether those bytes still run against a platform that moved.  This row is
; the part that is checkable, and it is compared for EQUALITY, never parsed
; -- the platform's existing rule for release strings.
;
; 0.5.2 is what this bundle's 72 specs are green against.  Running it on
; anything else should be a decision someone made, not something that
; happened.
(requires-release "0.5.2")

(entry "run.x")
